  "source": "The Swedish National Council for Crime Prevention (Brå)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: The number of abuse/violent crimes taking place outdoors against persons 15 years  and older, reported to the police with unknown offender per 100,000 inhabitants aged 15 and above according to the crime codes 0355, 0357, 0375, 0377, 9317, 9319, 9341 and 9343.The indicator is divided into 7 police regions. Before 2015, the police were organized into 21 police authorities. This has been corrected retroactively in accordance with the current police regions."
  ]
